🔐 JWT Employee Management — Complete Flow
-------------------------------------------------------------
Start MySQL
-----------------------
Start MySQL first.
Create the database only once:

CREATE DATABASE jwt_employee_db;
Your application.properties:
---------------------------------
spring.application.name=jwt-employee-management

spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/jwt_employee_db
spring.datasource.username=root
spring.datasource.password=root

spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
spring.jpa.show-sql=true
spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.format_sql=true

server.port=8080

Replace root password if necessary.

Start Spring Boot
-----------------------------
Run:
JwtApplication.java

Wait for:
Tomcat started on port 8080
Started JwtApplication
Now the application is running.


STEP 1 — REGISTER new USER
---------------------------
This is done when creating a new account.
Postman

Method
POST
URL
http://localhost:8080/auth/register

Authorization
No Auth
Body

Select:
Body → raw → JSON
Send:

{
    "username": "subham",
    "password": "12345"
}

Expected response
User registered successfully

Now the user exists in the users table.



STEP 2- LOGIN THE EXIT USER
-----------------------------
METHOD POST 
URL----http://localhost:8080/auth/login

BODY-JSON PEST IT USERNAME AND PASSWORD
----------------------------------------
PAST IT
{
    "username": "subham",
    "password": "12345"
}
THEN CLICK SEND

IT SHOULD GIVE LIKE THAT
---------------------------
{
    "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..."
}

STEP-3 FOR DOING OPERATIONS
------------------------------
AFTER GETTING TOKEN COPY THEN DO

METHOD GET 
URL--http://localhost:8080/employees

GO TO Authorization → Bearer Token
Paste your token WHICH EXACT YOU GET NOT PEST (""):
-----------------
eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJzdWJoYW0i...

THEN ADD MANULY DATA IN YOUR DATA BASE 
THEN CLICK SEND YOU GET 
[
    {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "Rahul Das",
        "department": "CSE",
        "salary": 20000.0,
        "email": "rahul12@gmail.com"
    }
]



Then you can perform CRUD
----------------------------
1.Add Employee
----------------
POST http://localhost:8080/employees

Authorization → Bearer Token → same JWT

Body:

{
    "name": "Amit Kumar",
    "department": "Java",
    "salary": 35000,
    "email": "amit@gmail.com"
}

2.View All
-------------------
GET http://localhost:8080/employees

3.View One
--------------------
GET http://localhost:8080/employees/1

4.Update
----------------
PUT http://localhost:8080/employees/1

Body:

{
    "name": "Rahul Das Updated",
    "department": "Java Full Stack",
    "salary": 45000,
    "email": "rahulupdated@gmail.com"
}
5.Delete
---------------
DELETE http://localhost:8080/employees/1


